  "Question": "If \\(8^x=32,\\) then \\(x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac53\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac32\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac35\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac14\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Since \\(8=2^3\\) and \\(32=2^5\\), rewriting with base \\(2\\) lets us compare the exponents. The power-of-a-power rule gives\n\\[\n8^x=32\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n(2^3)^x=2^5\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n2^{3x}=2^5.\n\\]\nBecause \\(2>1\\), its powers strictly increase as the real exponent increases. Thus equal powers of \\(2\\) must have equal exponents, so \\(3x=5\\). Dividing by \\(3\\) gives the unique solution \\(\\boxed{x=\\frac53}\\), choice B.",
